  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 130 PM MST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nSaturday...Ridging aloft bulges across Wyoming, helping to produce \nsurface lee troughing and a warming trend. Continued dry with a lack \nof low and mid level moisture.\n\nSunday...Well pronounced ridging aloft continues, keeping us mild \nand dry. 700 mb temperatures near 6 Celsius will yield maximum \ntemperatures from the upper 50s to upper 60s.\n\nMonday-Tuesday...Dry and mild weather will continue with westerly \nflow aloft and only a weak positively tilted shortwave trough aloft \nmoving across Wyoming on Tuesday.\n\nWednesday-Thursday...Ridging aloft reasserts itself across the Great \nBasin States from western Montana to Utah, keeping our counties in \nnortherly flow aloft. 700 mb temperatures from 0 to 2 Celsius will \nhelp produce high temperatures from the mid 50s to mid 60s.",
